    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add a text-effect (a.k.a. flower / text effect) segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --content TEXT      Text content shown inside the effect\r\n          --resource TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Text-effect resource (vimo://<id> / local path)\r\n          --name TEXT         Text-effect name\r\n          --category-id TEXT  Text-effect category id\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --text-type TEXT    Material text type: text/subtitle/lyrics\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add a text-effect (flower / text effect) segment with content\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft text effect add --resource vimo://123 --content \"Hello\"\r\n  # Add a subtitle-typed text-effect segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft text effect add --resource vimo://123 --content \"Hi\" --text-type subtitle\r\n",
